<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    LCS: deliberately blank splash icon.

    The system splash and the in-app branded overlay were both drawing the
    launcher logo, one after the other, which read as two splash screens. They
    could not be made to match: ic_launcher_foreground is an adaptive-icon
    foreground whose glyph occupies only the inner ~2/3 of the image, and the
    platform crops to that safe zone while a plain Image composable does not —
    so the same asset renders about a third smaller in the overlay. The exact
    crop and container size also vary by API level and OEM, so matching them is
    guesswork.

    Instead the system splash draws nothing but the white field, and
    LcsBrandedSplashOverlay is the only thing that ever draws the logo. One
    logo, one wordmark, one splash.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="@android:color/transparent" />
    <size
        android:width="192dp"
        android:height="192dp" />
</shape>
